[center][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]A quickhack editor for Cyberpunk 2077, in VS Code.[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[center]Open any quickhack and change its name, icon, costs and effects. Make new ones from the game's own status effects.[/center]
[center][/center]
[center][size=3]One of the VS Code tools from the Edgemodders community. They all work together, with optional AI assistants.[/size][/center]
[line]

[quote][size=4][b][color=#fcee0a](STATUS)[/color][/b][/size]
[b]This is not a game mod.[/b] It is an extension for VS Code, so install it there (steps below), not with Vortex. The quickhack mods it makes are game mods: they need TweakXL and ArchiveXL.[/quote]

(SCREENSHOT: the editor with a quickhack open)

[size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]WHAT IT DOES[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Open any quickhack[/b] from its own Quickhacks view, or by clicking one in REDcode, and see everything about it in plain words: name, icon, tier, RAM, upload time, cooldown, duration, damage and the effects it applies.
[*][b]Change it:[/b] texts, icons, costs and numbers, for one tier or the whole family.
[*][b]Make new ones:[/b] start from a game quickhack and add buffs, debuffs and attack features, taken from other quickhacks or from the game's status effects that work on enemies.
[*][b]A mod you can read:[/b] EDGEhack writes TweakXL and ArchiveXL files into your REDcode project, and REDcode packs it and starts the game.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]INSTALL[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://code.visualstudio.com/]VS Code[/url] 1.90 or later, and REDcode from the Marketplace.
[*]In VS Code, open the Extensions view (Ctrl+Shift+X), click ... at its top, choose Install from VSIX..., and pick the .vsix from this download.
[*]Open EDGEhack in the side bar.
[/list]

